PS5's RADV supports sparseBinding, sparseResidencyAliased, sparseResidencyBuffer, sparseResidencyImage2D,
residencyStandard2DBlockShape, shaderResourceMinLod, unaligned mip sizes, and filterMinmaxSingleComponentFormats,
and binds unbound tiles to a shared zero block without faulting. It lacks only PRT page bits
(shaderResourceResidency and residencyNonResidentStrict).

Patch 0001 allowed Feature Level 12_0+ while still reporting D3D12_TILED_RESOURCES_TIER_1, a combination that
never exists on Windows hardware (D3D12 mandates Tier 2 for FL 12_0). Modern D3D12 engines check
TiledResourcesTier >= 2 for transient-resource registration while creating CreateReservedResource transient
render targets on FL 12_0+, leaving the transient pool unpopulated and crashing on the first render-target bind.

Report D3D12_TILED_RESOURCES_TIER_2 (capped at Tier 2, never Tier 3/4) when all Tier 2 requirements except PRT
residency feedback are present, and guard VKD3D_SHADER_META_FLAG_USES_SPARSE_RESIDENCY on
device_info.features2.features.shaderResourceResidency directly so shaders using CheckAccessFullyMapped are still
refused cleanly at pipeline creation.

--- a/libs/vkd3d/device.c
+++ b/libs/vkd3d/device.c
@@ -8888,13 +8888,18 @@
             !device->queue_families[VKD3D_QUEUE_FAMILY_SPARSE_BINDING]->queue_count)
         return D3D12_TILED_RESOURCES_TIER_NOT_SUPPORTED;
 
-    if (!features->shaderResourceResidency || !features->shaderResourceMinLod ||
+    if (!features->shaderResourceMinLod ||
             sparse_properties->residencyAlignedMipSize ||
-            !sparse_properties->residencyNonResidentStrict ||
             !device->device_info.vulkan_1_2_properties.filterMinmaxSingleComponentFormats)
         return D3D12_TILED_RESOURCES_TIER_1;
 
-    if (!features->sparseResidencyImage3D ||
+    /* PS5: RADV has every Tier 2 capability except PRT residency feedback (shaderResourceResidency /
+     * residencyNonResidentStrict) and backs unbound tiles with a zero block. Report Tier 2 so FL 12_0+
+     * engines do not see an impossible FL 12_0 + Tier 1 mismatch, cap at Tier 2 without PRT, and guard
+     * shader sparse-residency queries on shaderResourceResidency at PSO validation. */
+    if (!features->shaderResourceResidency ||
+            !sparse_properties->residencyNonResidentStrict ||
+            !features->sparseResidencyImage3D ||
             !sparse_properties->residencyStandard3DBlockShape)
         return D3D12_TILED_RESOURCES_TIER_2;
 
@@ -10724,9 +10729,10 @@
     }
 
     if ((meta->flags & VKD3D_SHADER_META_FLAG_USES_SPARSE_RESIDENCY) &&
-            device->d3d12_caps.options.TiledResourcesTier < D3D12_TILED_RESOURCES_TIER_2)
+            (device->d3d12_caps.options.TiledResourcesTier < D3D12_TILED_RESOURCES_TIER_2 ||
+                    !device->device_info.features2.features.shaderResourceResidency))
     {
-        WARN("Attempting to use sparse residency query in shader %016"PRIx64", but this requires sparse tier 2.\n", meta->hash);
+        WARN("Attempting to use sparse residency query in shader %016"PRIx64", but this requires sparse tier 2 and shaderResourceResidency.\n", meta->hash);
         return false;
     }
 
